atars.githubusercontent.com/u/11870879?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/e3b0c442","html_url":"https://github.com/e3b0c442","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e3b0c442/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e3b0c442/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e3b0c442/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e3b0c442/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e3b0c442/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e3b0c442/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e3b0c442/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e3b0c442/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e3b0c442/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2017-05-26T18:14:35Z","updated_at":"2017-05-26T18:14:35Z","body":"> One inner chord has only one task \r\n\r\nI think this may be the key. I dynamically generate my chords and they may have anywhere from 1-∞ members, and I noticed that when the chord has only one member, the result is not passed to the callback wrapped in a list.\r\n\r\nUpon looking at the release notes, I discovered the following:\r\n> A chord where the header group only consists of a single task is now turned into a simple chain.\r\n\r\nI think this conversion is failing to wrap the result in a list as would happen if there were multiple tasks in the header. If your callback code is expecting to handle that list, you would run into errors. Complicating matters is the case (like mine) where the chord task result is itself a list.\r\n\r\nNot sure if this specific finding has been reported elsewhere, I found this bug in that search.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/celery/celery/issues/comments/304352942/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes"